          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "цена (tsená) from Proto-Slavic cěna — inherited. Vasmer relates it to Lithuanian kainà, \"price\", Avestan kaēnā-, \"retribution\", and Greek poinḗ, \"penalty\", the source of English pain."
            }
          ]
        },
